        {
            "id": "b026ea0e-fee6-49b3-bc46-4d6e2fd79179",
            "category": "Cross-platform Application",
            "title": "SmileSys",
            "date": [
                {
                    "year": 2025,
                    "month": 12,
                    "day": 12,
                    "item": "01",
                    "progress": "June 2026"
                }
            ],
            "image": "../res/img/Coding Clipart.png",
            "images": [
                {
                    "src": "res/img/smilesys_1.png"
                }
            ],
            "description": [
                "Prototype School Project",
                "Client-side is written on .NET MAUI 9, while the server-side was written on ASP.NET Core 9",
                "Runs on Android and Windows. It was originally intended for iOS, but the requirements to develop an iOS system was unfeasible since it needed a real Mac computer.",
                "An application used to manage patient records with syncing capabilities based on a System Requirement Specification from a clinic.",
                "This school project tremendously lacked proper coordination with other developers. This effectively let myself develop the whole system alone for a limited amount of time for six months: the client front-end, the client back-end, and the server back-end while also ensuring that it will run cross-platform, and also the most of the paper works (e.g. diagrams, Gantt chart, system architecture, etc.) For the same reason, the front-end was tremendously underdeveloped.",
                "The lack of coordination was caused by the lack of willingness of my teammates to cooperate and listen. I was the project leader of all aspects of the project and there were only three group members.",
                "Many portions of the application and web server was heavily AI-generated, making it extremely unstable, unreliable, and insecure.",
                "Many portions of the system is undocumented.",
                "Was shut down immediately after testing by clients with one patient data due to several security issues. The security flaws were discovered during the testing period. All the data stored on the system were handed over to the clients through a cloud storage and all the data left on the server were erased immediately. It was treated like a garbage on a dumpster fire by myself and shall forever be.",
                "Not used for production environments.",
                "It was a giant blob of many, many mistakes from many, many aspects. From overreliance to AI during the system development, improper communication, to improper leadership. It was also a pinnacle of unprofessionalism."
            ],
            "hidden": false
        },
